.TH SDL_WaitEvent 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_WaitEvent \- Wait indefinitely for the next available event.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_events.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_WaitEvent(SDL_Event *event);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
If
.BR event
is not NULL, the next event is removed from the queue and stored in the
.BR SDL_Event
structure pointed to by
.BR event \[char46]
.PP
As this function may implicitly call
.BR SDL_PumpEvents (),
you can only call this function in the thread that initialized the video subsystem\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I event
the
.BR SDL_Event
structure to be filled in with the next event from the queue, or NULL\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success or false if there was an error while waiting for events; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function should only be called on the main thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_PollEvent (3),
.BR SDL_PushEvent (3),
.BR SDL_WaitEventTimeout (3)
